WEBVTT

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.130
Hey, Playmaker.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.560
Come with me.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.530
What do you mean?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.300
Be one with me.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.000
Change your consciousness 
into data and fuse with me.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.970
Only you can stop me.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.530
If we're one, lifespans won’t matter.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:40.480
We should be able to create a different 
future than Bohman or Lightning, right?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.720
We can live in the network 
world for eternity.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:46.730
Ai…

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.700
Playmaker…

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.630
I can’t do that.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:04.080
Even if we become one, that's 
not the solution you're seeking.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.550
We only have one life, one consciousness.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.780
If you and I fuse, I won’t be me.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.750
And you won’t be you.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.920
Ai, living has no solutions.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.300
When we're in pain, we search 
for a solution to feel better.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.730
A concise, absolute solution.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:30.470
But if there's a solution...

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.940
It’s that there are no solutions.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.050
There are no absolutes in this world.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:44.180
Even if we think there is, it'll only 
makes us feel better for a moment.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.850
If there are no absolutes, what’s left?

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.160
Bonds.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.590
Bonds between individuals.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.040
Bonds between one another.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.000
That’s all there is.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.630
That also changes with time.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.700
A huge trigger can cause a huge change.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.010
Bonds may be severed.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.910
But new bonds can also be formed.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.110
So living is a series of bonds.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.580
That’s what life is!

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.460
I have to do that forever?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.390
Yes.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.030
That's a lot of work.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.060
Yeah.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.790
And you can’t do that 
unless you’re strong.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.260
That’s why people become stronger.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.800
That occasionally leads to conflicts.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.270
But even if that happens, 
we have to keep fighting.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:44.770
Keep searching for bonds, 
even if there's no solution.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.280
I see.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:51.120
I was thinking too logically, like an AI.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:55.590
You can’t rush living.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.830
But I don’t want to keep 
fighting if there's no solution.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:07.030
Since I lost the desire to 
fight, I'm destined to vanish.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.770
Ai…

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.340
Sigh…  He dumped me.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.170
But the path we're each taking is set.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.010
Bring it on, Playmaker.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.400
Let’s end this.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:32.700
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:03:51.290 --> 00:04:00.660
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:10.610
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:15.840
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:24.390
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:29.530
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:35.200
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.500
calling  With invisible wings

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:50.110
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.510
There are no monsters on my field.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.750
And zero cards in my hand.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:10.460
This draw will definitely decide my fate.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.640
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.860
I activate the Continuous Trap, A.I.Q!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:28.770
While this card is in the Spell & Trap Zone, 
we can only Link Summon once per turn!

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.510
A card that limits Link Summoning!

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:37.980
You only have one chance to 
bring out a Link Monster.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:43.250
I activate the Ritual Spell, Cynet 
Ritual’s effect from my graveyard!

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.940
When there are no monsters on my field...

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:52.960
...I banish this card and a Ritual Monster from 
my graveyard to Special Summon two Cynet Tokens!

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.340
I banish Cynet Ritual and Cyberse Magician!

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:04.310
I activate the spell card, Drastic Draw!

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:13.890
When I have at least two monsters, I banish 
all monsters on my field to draw three cards!

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:21.930
When there are no monsters on my field, I 
can Special Summon Linkslayer from my hand!

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.790
Then I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:33.710
When there’s a Cyberse on my field, I 
Special Summon Backup Secretary from my hand!

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:40.250
Linkslayer, Cyberse Wizard, 
Backup Secretary…

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.380
They're making me feel nostalgic.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.350
I activate Borreload Furious 
Dragon’s effect from my graveyard!

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:54.330
I banish this card to Special Summon 
a Dark Link Monster from my graveyard!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:07:00.060
The Special Summoned monster can’t 
activate its effects this turn.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.300
Resurrect, Firewall Dragon Darkfluid!

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.800
Here I go, Ai!

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.960
This is my final Link Summon!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.340
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.780
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.780
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.690
Circuit combine!

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.580
Seize the wind that connects 
to the unseen world!

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.960
Link Summon!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.600
Link 4 Accesscode Talker!

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.220
Accesscode Talker…

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:42.670
You had no monsters or cards in your hand, 
but you’ve brought it back this far.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.540
Impressive.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.380
Accesscode Talker’s effect activates!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:55.500
When a Link Monster is used to summon it, it 
gains 1000 ATK for each of its Link Markers!

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.150
I select Link 5 Darkfluid!

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:04.100
Therefore, Accesscode gains 5000 ATK!

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:11.640
But that's far from enough ATK against 
The Arrival Cyberse @Ignister.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.370
I know!

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.870
Accesscode Talker’s effect activates!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:22.440
I banish a Link Monster from my graveyard 
to destroy a card on your field!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:28.720
As long as the banished monster has a 
different Attribute, I can keep using this effect!

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:34.860
There are six monsters in Playmaker’s 
graveyard with different Attributes.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.160
I banish the Earth Attribute 
Transcode from my graveyard

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.760
to destroy the Field 
Spell, Ignister A.I.Land!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.470
Access Integration!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.610
So annoying!

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:57.820
When an effect destroys Ignister A.I.Land, 
I have to destroy all monsters on my field.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:04.160
But due to Gatchiri @Ignister’s effect, 
monsters on my field

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.150
aren’t destroyed one time this turn!

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:12.560
But The Arrival’s ATK decrease!

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.160
I activate Accesscode’s effect again!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.470
I banish the Water Attribute 
Splash Mage from my graveyard!

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.040
I destroy Gatchiri @Ignister!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.310
Access Integration!

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:34.110
The Arrival loses more ATK!

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.290
I activate the destroyed Gatchiri’s effect!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:47.140
On the turn it leaves the field, your 
effects can't affect one of my monsters!

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.620
I select The Arrival!

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:56.540
Now you can't use Accesscode’s 
effect to destroy The Arrival.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.800
I'll use the effect for a third time!

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:05.350
I banish the Fire Attribute Proxy F 
Magician to destroy Gussari @Ignister!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:08.090
Access Integration!

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:14.200
The Arrival loses more ATK!

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:20.500
I banish the Wind Attribute Exslayer 
from my graveyard to destroy Darkwight!

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:27.810
I banish the Light Attribute Linkross 
from my graveyard to destroy A.I.Q!

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:33.920
I banish the Dark Attribute Decode 
Talker to destroy CompromA.I.se!

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.650
The Arrival has 7000 ATK.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:43.390
Only The Arrival and Accesscode 
remain on the field.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.660
Seems it's time for the finale.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.270
Ai…

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:50.660
Let's battle!

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:56.100
Accesscode Talker attacks The 
Arrival Cyberse @Ignister!

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:59.300
I activate Gussari’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:05.780
When my @Ignister Link Monster battles, by 
banishing this card from my graveyard...

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.860
...both our monsters’ ATK become 3000!

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.320
Strike back, The Arrival!

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.980
When the battle ends...

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:42.980
...I can Special Summon an @Ignister 
Link Monster from my graveyard

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:45.450
with fewer Link Markers than my monster.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:51.770
I use Gussari’s effect to Special Summon 
Dark Templar @Ignister from my graveyard.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:57.630
Now I'm the only one with 
a monster on the field.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.770
The spell card, Cynet Closure’s effect!

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:07.070
When my Cyberse Link Monster destroys 
your Link Monster in battle...

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:11.360
...I return a facedown card that was 
banished from my deck to my graveyard!

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:15.480
I return the trap card, Recoded 
Alive to my graveyard!

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:21.850
That’s the card he banished 
using Cynet Closure’s effect.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:25.560
So it was Recoded Alive.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.630
Recoded Alive’s effect from my graveyard!

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:32.630
When I don't have a monster 
in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:38.560
...I banish this card to Special 
Summon my banished Decode Talker!

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.620
Decode Talker...

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:47.910
But Dark Templar can’t be destroyed 
by a monster with the same ATK.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:53.320
If Decode Talker attacks, 
only it will be destroyed!

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.990
I end my turn.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:01.930
Ai, did you run a simulation of our duel?

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:04.700
No.  That would be lame.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.430
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:55.880 --> 00:14:02.390
Hey Playmaker, was I a good partner?

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:06.540
Yeah.  You were the best partner.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:10.230
I see.  That’s good.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.580
Dark Templar attacks Decode Talker!

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:22.810
I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, TA.I. Strike!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:31.220
The controller of the monster destroyed in this 
battle will take damage equal to its original ATK!

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:36.620
Farewell, Playmaker.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:41.180
I activate the Continuous Trap, Code 
Hack’s effect from my graveyard!

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:46.460
When a Code Talker battles, 
by banishing this card...

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:54.710
...your spell or trap card’s activation is 
negated, and the Code Talker gains 700 ATK!

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:56.010
What?

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.540
Decode...

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.380
...End!

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.160
Ai!

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.370
Ai...

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.840
I lost.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:31.580
You would've won if you didn’t 
activate TA.I. Strike.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:39.320
I did think you were up to something 
when you brought out Decode Talker.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:44.030
But I thought it'd be fine anyway.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:46.790
Because I couldn’t choose.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:54.520
As I told you, I didn't 
fight you in the simulation.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.740
But at that time…

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.740
When I lived in the simulation’s future…

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.870
I saw it.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:20.620
What my existence will lead to.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:26.660
You get dragged into it and perish.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:35.170
I can’t choose that future.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.640
Ai…

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:42.420
As promised, I’ll return everything.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:57.030
I’m going to vanish.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:00.030
I’m starting to get scared.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:04.440
Everyone will forget me eventually.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.320
Oh, I get it now.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:12.780
If you have bonds, no one will forget you.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.750
I won’t forget you.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:20.620
Hey, can I ask you one final thing?

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:29.230
You lazily gave me the name 
Ai, but I really like it.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:35.230
If this name has a definition, 
what do you think it is?

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:41.210
"Ai" means "to love people."

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:44.210
I think so too.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:48.490
Now I understand that definition.

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:53.740
Bye, Play-  Yusaku.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:55.690
I loved you.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.080
Ai!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:29.360
Ai!

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:36.140
Three months later

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:45.200
Okay, your order's coming soon!

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:49.210
Brother!  Two hot dogs and coffees!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.620
Okay!

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:54.180
It's nice that your brother is healthy again.

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:57.960
Yeah.  He can now live in peace.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.150
We’ll make up for the time we lost.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.860
Aoi, it’s thanks to you all.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.400
No, I didn’t do anything.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:14.870
It was Fujiki and the others.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:18.340
By the way, any contact from Fujiki?

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.320
None.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.070
Not since his final duel with Ai.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:25.480
I see.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:29.810
He always protected what's dear to me.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:34.030
Same here.  He’s our hero.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:39.920
Are you keeping your stand here?

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.100
Yeah.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:45.760
He'd be sad if he didn’t 
have a home to return to.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.870
My brother says the same thing.

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:59.880
So shut this and that.  And 
make the data flow from here.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.460
CEO Zaizen!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.670
Any glitches in LINK VRAINS?

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.850
Everything's working smoothly!

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:20.800
LINK VRAINS has become the central 
station that connects various worlds.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:24.730
Meaning there's infinite possibilities!

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:29.770
It’s our mission to protect LINK VRAINS.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:33.240
Until he comes back home.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.200
They'll eat us!

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:46.860
LINK VRAINS has grown too much!

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:50.290
C'mon!  Go back and search for scoops!

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:53.300
That’s crazy!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.770
Brother, handle the one on the left!

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:01.740
I know.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.710
Be careful, Emma.

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:15.290
Onizuka did it!

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.090
Onizuka is the champion!

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.880
Keep bringing it on!

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.330
Go Onizuka will take you on!

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:31.270
LINK VRAINS is growing rapidly.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:33.740
It’ll become bigger and bigger.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.960
It's not only LINK VRAINS.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.590
The network will keep expanding too.

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:42.710
That’s why they need observers like us.

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:48.450
It's how the Hanoi can atone for our crimes.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.970
I'm scared...

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:57.490
Don’t worry!  Let’s go!

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:00.500
Into the VRAINS!

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.160
Wow!

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:14.850
This is LINK VRAINS.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.850
A new world for people!

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:21.820
That’s Soulburner!

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.970
And he has a girlfriend!

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:31.160
I’ll give my max to meet someone!

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:36.370
Takeru, you’re cool!

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:39.370
Don’t be silly!

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:44.840
Besides, there’s someone 
cooler than me here.

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:47.080
Really?  I want to meet him!

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:51.180
Well, he’s on a journey right now.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:52.430
Really?

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:54.790
Yeah.  But…

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:02.060
Will he return?

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:06.800
Of course.  Playmaker will definitely return.

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:09.280
And much stronger!

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.910
Into the VRAINS!

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:33.460
Huh?

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:42.200
Yu-Gi-Oh! Animated Series
20th Anniversary

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:46.840
New animated series in production

00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:51.900
On air in 2020
